[C1] PASS amplification factors on u' = lambda u: rk1 1+z; rk2 to z^2/2; rk3 to z^3/6; rk3s4 to z^3/6 + z^4/48; max error 2.2e-16
[C2] PASS fitted order on a nonlinear ODE, n = 40, 80, 160 steps: rk1 1.01, rk2 2.01, rk3 3.02, rk3s4 3.01
[C3] PASS each stage is a convex combination of u0 and a forward-Euler step; SSP coefficient C = min over stages of (Euler weight)/w2: rk1 C=1, rk2 C=1, rk3 C=1, rk3s4 C=2
[C4] PASS the stage values stay nonnegative up to dt = C: rk3 nonnegative for dt <= 1; rk3s4 nonnegative for dt <= 2
[C5] PASS the stage values of Derivation steps 1-4 are the exact stage product; the first power of Z whose coefficient differs from e^Z gives the order: rk3s4 last stage Z**4/48 + Z**3/6 + Z**2/2 + Z + 1; orders rk1 1, rk2 2, rk3 3, rk3s4 3
[C6] PASS every stage fraction c^(s)_FE is 1 for rk1, rk2, rk3 and 2 for rk3s4, so c_SSP = min_s c^(s)_FE = 1, 1, 1, 2: rk1 1; rk2 1, 1; rk3 1, 1, 1; rk3s4 2, 2, 2, 2
[C7] PASS at the same SSP guarantee rk3s4 takes a step c_SSP = 2 times that of rk3; per operator evaluation it advances 2/4 against 1/3, 3/2 times as far: step ratio 2, per evaluation 3/2
